{
  "description": "Closed vocabulary of skill tags used by the synthetic data set (personas, vacancy requirements, search queries). Each tag has display aliases that may appear in CV or GitHub text. Aliases of tags flagged \"ambiguous\" are short or are also common English words (Go, R, C, Swift, Spring, Express, ...): drift checks must match them case-sensitively and only in technical contexts. \"family\" lists the role families (vacancy ids) the tag naturally belongs to; the persona generator uses it to pick plausible filler skills. Tags without a family (git, agile) are generic. Experience tags (kind \"experience\", no aliases, ids exp-*) express \"N+ years in a field\" requirements: a requirement such as \"5+ years backend\" is { tags: [\"exp-backend\"], minYears: 5 }. A persona gets the tag on every role held in that field, so its years are the summed months of those roles. They never appear in prose, so text checks skip tags without aliases.",
